    "serial": {
        "baud_rate": 38400,
        "comments": "JP6 (5 pins) represents one serial port (3.3V), the only JP with a header soldered. When looking on the LEDs (front) and having the power and ethernet ports on the back JP6 is on the right and has the following pin-out from left to right:\n\n  *TX\n  *GND\n  *Vcc (3.3V)\n  *GND\n  *RX \n\nRefer to the DSL-624T's [[dsl-624t#serial]] section for the correct way to interface it with a DTE over an RS-232 serial port.\n\nThe bootloader is using 38400 baud, 8 bits, no parity, 1 stop-bit (38400 8n1):\n<code>\nADAM2 Revision 0.22.02_b04_Mar 10 2005\n(C) Copyright 1996-2003 Texas Instruments Inc. All Rights Reserved.\n(C) Copyright 2003 Telogy Networks, Inc.                                     \nUsage: setmfreq [-d] [-s sys_freq, in MHz] [cpu_freq, in MHz]                \nMemory optimization Complete!                                                \n                                                                             \nAdam2_AR7DB >                                                                \nPress any key to abort OS load, or wait 7 seconds for OS to boot...          \n</code>\n\n",
        "connector": "JP6",
        "data_parity_stop": "8N1",
